Data and Storage settings while creating a SageMaker User Profile.
=================================================================


1. AutoMountHomeEFS 📁

EFS = Elastic File System

It is cloud file storage that SageMaker can use for files such as:

Jupyter notebooks 📓
Python code 💻
Datasets 📊
Model files 🧠

Your screen has “Inherit settings from domain” selected.

That means:

SageMaker Domain Settings
          ↓
User Profile automatically uses
the same EFS/storage settings

For a beginner, leaving this as the default is usually simplest.

===

2. Customize Studio UI

This option lets you set different EFS storage and data settings specifically for this user profile.

Normally, you don't need to change it unless different users require different storage configurations.

=====

3. CustomPosixUserConfig 👤

This is an advanced Linux user configuration.

It can control things such as the Linux user ID/group ID used inside the SageMaker environment.

For normal learning and basic SageMaker use, you can leave this disabled.

Simple flow
Step 1 → General Settings 👤
Step 2 → Configure Applications 📓
Step 3 → Customize Studio UI 🎛️
Step 4 → Data and Storage 💾  ← You are here
Step 5 → Review and Create ✅

For this training setup, the instructor appears to be leaving the default settings and then clicking Next.

